  "reputation": {
    "summary": "A DAC DIY favourite for I/V: DAC current enters the low-impedance inverting input and the TZ node feeds a buffer, usually without global feedback. The long diyAudio thread 'Using the AD844 as an I/V' calls it the 'best opamp based I/V so far by a long way' and rates it above the OPA627. These are forum opinions, not measurements.",
    "sonic_descriptors": [],
    "typical_uses": [
      "Open-loop I/V for current-output DACs, buffered by OPA627",
      "2–3 paralleled per channel for lower I/V impedance",
      "High-speed video and pulse amplification",
      "Current-conveyor (CCII+) building block"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "Feedback resistor sets bandwidth; a capacitor directly in the feedback path invites oscillation.",
      "Open-loop TZ use leaves gain, linearity and DC offset uncorrected by feedback.",
      "6.5 mA per part adds up when several are paralleled.",
      "Only SMD package is SOIC-16W; no 8-lead SOIC for drop-in swaps.",
      "Praise comes from subjective forum listening."
    ],
    "sources": [
      "https://www.diyaudio.com/forums/digital-line-level/227677-using-ad844.html",
      "https://diyaudio.com/forums/digital-line-level/227677-using-ad844-81.html",
      "https://www.diyaudio.com/community/threads/using-the-ad844-as-an-i-v.227677/page-86",
      "https://www.diyaudio.com/community/threads/using-the-ad844-as-an-i-v.227677/page-23",
      "https://www.diyaudio.com/community/threads/using-the-ad844-as-an-i-v.227677/page-121"
    ]
  },
  "counterfeit_notes": "No AD844-specific counterfeit reports, but remarked eBay/AliExpress op-amps are well documented (Hackaday, Super-Freq). Buy from authorized distributors; be wary of loose 'AD844AN/JN' DIPs sold as new, since current production is AD844ANZ.",
  "alternatives": [
    "AD811 (ADI current feedback)",
    "OPA861 / OPA860 (TI diamond transistor)",
    "OPA627 / OPA827 (voltage-feedback I/V)",
    "Discrete common-base / CCII I/V"
  ],
